WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:04.970
For its fourth installment, the Insidious
franchise takes another step back in time.

00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:09.519
We see one of Elise Rainier's earliest childhood
experiences with the other side—and then

00:00:09.519 --> 00:00:14.500
we see her as a full-grown ghost-hunter who's
made to revisit her past in cruel and surprising

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:15.500
ways.

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:19.699
While the story is mostly a standalone adventure
for the spiritual psychic, The Last Key still

00:00:19.699 --> 00:00:23.890
draws on the mythology of the series, and
features some of the central players of the

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:26.529
franchise in fun and fresh new ways.

00:00:26.529 --> 00:00:31.109
Let's take a look at how Insidious: The Last
Key explores Elise's devastating backstory

00:00:31.109 --> 00:00:34.480
and wraps things up on a note of continuity.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:38.390
Pattern of possession
In childhood, Elise is tormented by more than

00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:40.860
just the spirits that occupy her family home.

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:45.219
Her prison guard father is also heavy-handed
with punishment, to the point of abuse.

00:00:45.219 --> 00:00:49.800
Clearly deranged, he insists he can beat the
ghostly visions out of her and fears her supernatural

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:50.809
gifts.

00:00:50.809 --> 00:00:54.770
Summoned back to the property in her later
years by the home's new occupant, Ted Garza,

00:00:54.770 --> 00:00:58.530
she discovers he's kidnapped and tortured
a woman in the basement for months.

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:00.460
He claims something has invaded his mind…

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:02.360
"He's in my head."

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:05.080
But he's still ultimately done away with by
Specs.

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:09.520
Afterwards, Elise continues to explore and
uncover more terrible secrets about the history

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:14.050
of the home, including her own father's similar
abduction and slaughter of a woman in that

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:15.210
very spot.

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:19.330
Elise realizes both men were possessed by
the demon that terrorized her in her youth,

00:01:19.330 --> 00:01:23.250
and instead of getting revenge on her ghost
dad in The Further, she decides not to feed

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:24.720
the demon herself.

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:28.760
It's not clear that all of her father's bad
behaviors were due to the demonic force, but

00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:33.550
he does apologize to her in ghost form before
withering back into his spiritual cell.

00:01:33.550 --> 00:01:35.020
Weapon of love

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:37.730
The true big bad of the movie is the key monster.

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:42.250
Elise first runs into it in childhood after
her father banishes her to the basement, with

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:46.060
a voice summoning her to a keyhole that unlocks
the door to the demon's lair.

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:50.230
Her mother is the first true victim of that
mistake, as she attempts to rescue Elise from

00:01:50.230 --> 00:01:54.960
the basement but is instead strangled by the
nefarious spirit while Elise remains in a

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:56.350
state of demonic hypnosis.

00:01:56.350 --> 00:01:59.610
Her mother's passing is a tragedy for Elise
and her brother.

00:01:59.610 --> 00:02:03.610
A warm and loving parent, she'd given him
a whistle to blow if he ever felt scared of

00:02:03.610 --> 00:02:04.950
Elise's sightings.

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:09.390
As we see in Elise's older years, the whistle
was lost for decades—but it pops up during

00:02:09.390 --> 00:02:13.360
her return to the old home, and it's used
by tortured spirits to guide her throughout

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:17.440
her battle, since the key demon deprives his
victims of the ability to speak.

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:18.580
"Shhhh…"

00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:23.280
When Elise confronts the demon in its lair,
it outmaneuvers her and deprives her of her

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:24.280
voice, too.

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:28.250
But she finds the whistle in time to summon
the spirit of her mother, who's able to vanquish

00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:31.090
the beast through the sheer power of her love
and light.

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:34.750
It's not clear if Elise's mother will ever
escape the otherworldly prison below that

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:38.340
house, but she does seem at peace when Elise
departs.

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:41.560
Coaching herself
One of the most surprising encounters Elise

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:46.050
experiences during her time in The Further
is when she runs into herself as a child in

00:02:46.050 --> 00:02:47.050
the basement.

00:02:47.050 --> 00:02:51.200
She doesn't tell the child version of herself
who she is, but does insist that young Elise

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:55.190
use her gifts to help people, despite her
father's tyrannical treatment.

00:02:55.190 --> 00:02:58.830
If only she'd been able to tip off the child
that the girl she spots in the laundry room

00:02:58.830 --> 00:03:02.480
at the age of 16 is very real, she might have
been able to save Anna.

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:03.480
Alas.

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:06.830
She does at least encourage her to use her
nightmares for the betterment of the world—and

00:03:06.830 --> 00:03:10.650
to never back down from demons, otherworldly
or otherwise.

00:03:10.650 --> 00:03:12.230
The family business

00:03:12.230 --> 00:03:16.440
Although Elise's brother is none too thrilled
to see her again, decades after she'd escaped

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:20.050
their father's menacing clutches, he doesn't
have a choice but to welcome her once she

00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:21.720
rescues his daughters.

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:25.569
After Elise informs Christian that she found
his old whistle in the home, he decides the

00:03:25.569 --> 00:03:27.690
relic is important enough to track down.

00:03:27.690 --> 00:03:31.400
Problem is, his youngest daughter Melissa
is summoned down to the basement by the key

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:35.980
demon, who makes short order of adding Elise's
niece to its collection of victims.

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:39.819
Elise senses the attack and returns to the
property, promising to find her.

00:03:39.819 --> 00:03:44.040
After she's temporarily incapacitated below,
though, the other sister Imogen decides to

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:48.880
try her own hand at psychic work and is lulled
into a state of hypnosis by Tucker and Specs.

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:50.760
"I can see things too."

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:54.680
She's there on a rescue mission, but it's
Elise who ultimately leads the two girls back

00:03:54.680 --> 00:03:58.760
to safety, and Christian is grateful for her
salvation of his daughters.

00:03:58.760 --> 00:04:03.050
Meanwhile, Imogen has now tapped into her
own paranormal gifts, and Elise's legacy can

00:04:03.050 --> 00:04:04.970
maybe live on through another generation.

00:04:04.970 --> 00:04:09.670
And that's very, very important to the franchise
as a whole because the movie finishes with

00:04:09.670 --> 00:04:12.910
a direct link to the timeline of the original
Insidious movies.

00:04:12.910 --> 00:04:16.890
Elise dreams about a boy named Dalton being
haunted by the red-faced demon we came to

00:04:16.890 --> 00:04:20.320
know so well in the earlier installments and
sees Renai [like "Renee"] and Josh, lying

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:23.370
in bed and lamenting the unknown that's troubling
their child.

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:27.780
Elise awakens to receive a call from Lorraine,
who reminds her that she helped her son Josh,

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:31.690
as we saw in the flashback events of Insidious
2, and now the same thing is happening to

00:04:31.690 --> 00:04:32.690
Dalton.

00:04:32.690 --> 00:04:36.120
That's the catalyst for the events of the
first Insidious, of course, when Elise helps

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:40.020
Dalton escape from The Further, only to be
strangled by Josh, who's been possessed by

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:42.690
the same demon that haunted him as a child.

00:04:42.690 --> 00:04:46.940
Insidious 2 left off with Elise still working
her demon-battling magic, following Tucker

00:04:46.940 --> 00:04:49.120
and Specs to new spectral assignments.

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:53.160
But with the added element of Imogen, a new
medium who can work with Elise from the earthly

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:57.750
plane, the ghostbusting business might not
be done for the Insidious team just yet.

00:04:57.750 --> 00:04:59.020
Thanks for watching!

00:04:59.020 --> 00:05:01.620
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:03.870
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

